AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::repay()
├── when market is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused for PAUSE_TYPE
├── when market is frozen but not paused
│   └── it should remain available
├── given invalid inputs
│   ├── when assets and shares are both zero
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when assets and shares are both nonzero
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   ├── when amount selection is invalid and onBehalf is also invalid
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput before checking creditAccount
│   ├── when onBehalf is not creditAccount
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketUnauthorizedAccount
│   ├── when onBehalf is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketUnauthorizedAccount
│   ├── when assets exceeds repayable debt
│   │   └── it should revert without changing accounting
│   └── when shares exceeds creditAccount borrow shares
│       └── it should revert without changing accounting
├── given repayment by assets
│   ├── it should calculate shares rounded down
│   ├── when a small asset repayment rounds to zero shares
│   │   └── it should reduce debt assets and burn tokens without reducing borrow shares
│   └── it should burn exactly the supplied assets from caller
├── given repayment by shares
│   ├── it should calculate assets rounded up
│   ├── it should permit repaying exactly all creditAccount borrow shares
│   └── it should burn the calculated assets from caller
├── given borrow token burn failure
│   ├── when caller balance is insufficient
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   ├── when market minter accounting cannot burn the amount
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   ├── when market lacks burner permission or borrow token is paused
│   │   └── it should revert atomically
│   └── when the token attempts reentrancy
│       └── it should reject reentrancy and revert atomically
└── given a valid repayment
    ├── when caller is creditAccount
    │   └── it should succeed
    ├── when caller is an authorized delegate
    │   └── it should succeed but burn tokens from the delegate
    ├── when caller is unrelated and not authorized
    │   └── it should succeed but burn tokens from that caller
    ├── it should accrue interest before calculating assets and shares
    ├── it should decrease totalBorrowed assets and shares
    ├── it should decrease only creditAccount borrowShares
    ├── it should not change totalSupply or collateralAssets
    ├── it should preserve claimableFeesAssets apart from interest added by pre-repayment accrual
    ├── it should not query the oracle or interact with Convex custody and rewards
    ├── when all borrow shares are repaid
    │   ├── it should leave the position eligible for collateral withdrawal
    │   └── it should preserve any residual totalBorrowed assets caused by virtual-share rounding
    ├── it should emit AccrueInterest before Repay
    └── it should return repaid assets and shares
